          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exploring Algebraic Identities"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.855,
            0.069,
            0.883,
            0.084
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "83"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.108,
            0.884,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that the volume of this cube is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( a + b ) ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Let us split this cube into smaller cubes and cuboids."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.155,
            0.925,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.111,
                0.155,
                0.925,
                0.703
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.325,
                0.71,
                0.673,
                0.728
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 4.10: Representation of the identity"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.728,
            0.625,
            0.745
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "( a + b ) ^ { 3 } = a ^ { 3 } + 3 a ^ { 2 } b + 3 a b ^ { 2 } + b ^ { 3 }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.756,
            0.884,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that the larger cube can be split into two cubes and six cuboids. The cubes have volumes, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b ^ { \\overline { { 3 } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cubic units, respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.795,
            0.885,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Amongst the other six cuboids, three have dimensions a units × a units "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\times \\textit { b }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units and other three have dimensions a units "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\times b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units × b units, and so their volumes are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { 2 } b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a b ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cubic units, respectively. Hence the total volume of the six cuboids is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 a ^ { 2 } b ^ { \\mathrm { ~ + ~ } } 3 a b ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
